{"groups":[{"members":["c1"],"primary":"c1","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act (criminal record screening limits)","requirement":"Housing providers may not ask about an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer. Limited exceptions apply for lifetime sex offender registration and for methamphetamine manufacture convictions on the premises of federally assisted housing. After a conditional offer, providers may consider only specified convictions within set look-back periods, and may withdraw the offer only after an individualized assessment showing a substantial, legitimate and nondiscriminatory interest, with written notice of the reasons and an opportunity to appeal.","key_value":"No criminal inquiry before a conditional offer; look-back after a conditional offer: 6 years (1st degree), 4 years (2nd/3rd degree), 1 year (4th degree); applicant may request the information relied on within 30 days and the provider must supply it free within 10 days","status":"in_force","effective_date":"2022-01-01","end_date":null,"citation":"P.L.2021, c.110 (N.J.S.A. 46:8-52 et seq.)","coverage_conditions":"Applies to housing providers offering a rental dwelling unit for residential purposes.","exemptions":"Excludes a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","conflict_note":null},{"members":["c3","c2"],"primary":"c3","title":"NJ Law Against Discrimination: source of lawful income / rent payment","requirement":"The LAD prohibits refusing to rent, or otherwise discriminating in renting housing, based on the source of lawful income or source of lawful rent payment a tenant uses. A landlord cannot deny a lawful Section 8 HUD voucher recipient the right to rent an apartment based solely on that source of income.","key_value":"Source of lawful income (including Section 8 HUD vouchers) is a protected basis and cannot be the sole basis for denying a rental","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 10:5-12(g) to (h) (New Jersey Law Against Discrimination, N.J.S.A. 10:5-1 et seq.)","coverage_conditions":"Applies to the sale or rental of real property, including rental housing.","exemptions":"Rental of a single apartment or flat in a two-family dwelling where the owner occupies the other unit as a residence; rental of a room or rooms by the owner or occupant of a one-family dwelling occupied by him/her as a residence; religious organization preference for persons of the same religion.","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
